/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003EGlobal\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003EData Type\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003ELand-based Station\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003EPeriod of Record\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003E1763\\u2013Present (Varies by Station)\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003EFile Format\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003Epdf\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003Etext (ascii)\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003Ecsv\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003Ejson\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003Exml\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CP\\u003EThe NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI) Past Weather Tool allows users to search for historical temperature, precipitation, snowfall, and snow depth data for individual weather stations across the United States, as well as many international locations. Stations are part of the \\u003CA\\u003EGHCN (Global Historical Climatology Network)-Daily\\u003C/A\\u003E dataset.\\u003C/P\\u003E\\u003CH2\\u003EAccess\\u003C/H2\\u003E\\u003CA\\u003EPast Weather Tool\\u003C/A\\u003E\\u003CH2\\u003EHow To\\u003C/H2\\u003E\\u003CUL\\u003E\\u003CLI\\u003EUse the search bar to enter a location of interest (e.g., city, address, zip code). Or, use the map to find a location by using zoom/pan or Shift\\u002BClick\\u002BDrag and then click \\u0022Search this area.\\u201D A set of stations from that location will be displayed (if any exist). Select the desired station from the list or from the map to view available daily data for that station.\\u003C/LI\\u003E\\u003CLI\\u003EAdjust the date in the \\u201CSelected Date\\u201D field and select a dataset (average temperature, maximum temperature, minimum temperature, precipitation, snowfall, or snow depth) to view a time series for that indicator.\\u003C/LI\\u003E\\u003CLI\\u003EAbove the time series, click the \\u201C1 year\\u201D button to view a time series for 1 year through the selected date. Click the button with the selected date to view the values on that date every year over the full period of record for that station (e.g., the average temperature every August 25 from 1962 to 2021 for Lakewood, CO).\\u003C/LI\\u003E\\u003CLI\\u003EUse the links below the time series to download the data or a PDF monthly weather report for that station.\\u003C/LI\\u003E\\u003CLI\\u003EFor more information, click the \\u201Ci\\u201D icon next to the station name. A popup will provide links to station history and further details through the \\u003CA\\u003EHistorical Observing Metadata Repository (HOMR)\\u003C/A\\u003E.\\u003C/LI\\u003E\\u003C/UL\\u003E\\u003CH2\\u003EDocumentation\\u003C/H2\\u003E\\u003CP\\u003EAll stations are part of the \\u003CA\\u003EGHCN (Global Historical Climatology Network)-Daily\\u003C/A\\u003E dataset. GHCN-Daily data may lag by a few days due to a comprehensive set of quality assurance checks. Only data with blank quality flags (i.e., that did not fail any quality assurance checks) are returned.\\u003C/P\\u003E\\u003CH3\\u003EPartner (s)\\u003C/H3\\u003E\\u003CDIV\\u003ERepresentative Image\\u003C/DIV\\u003E\\u003CP\\u003ESubscribe to NIDIS emails for the latest regional drought updates, webinars, and news. Or, sign up to receive drought alerts when the U.S. Drought Monitor or U.S. Drought Outlook updates for your city/zip code.\\u003C/P\\u003E\\u003CMETA description=\\u0022The NCEI Past Weather Tool allows users to search for historical temperature, precipitation, snowfall, and snow depth data for individual weather stations across the United States, as well as many international locations. Stations are part of the GHCN (Global Historical Climatology Network)-Daily dataset.\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C/META\\u003E\",\n        \"crawledAt\": \"2026-09-04T08:10:00.0000000Z\",\n        \"language\": \"en\",\n        \"isAdult\": false,\n        \"clickUrl\": \"https://api.microsoft.ai/ck/a?!\\u0026\\u0026p=a608dd3ff740f2147931c976cc21db055f02ba2f579349107709722544218ab6JmltdHM9MTc4ODU2NDY3MSZpZ3VpZD1kYmVlODQ4MS0wYTg2LTVkNWEtY2Q3OS1lOGYwNDQ4YmI2YTEmbGdtYXA9UDJOcFpEMHlOa0kxTTBaRU1EUTVNamswTXpORU9FRXhOalE0TURNeU9VSXhNVEJHUWlaaGNIQnVjejFFWlhaRmVDWnJQVEV3TURnbQ\\u0026ptn=10\\u0026ntb=1\\u0026u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZHJvdWdodC5nb3YvZGF0YS1tYXBzLXRvb2xzL25jZWktcGFzdC13ZWF0aGVyLXRvb2w\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Past Weather by Zip Code - Data Table | NOAA Climate.gov\",\n        \"url\": \"https://prod-01-asg-www-climate.woc.noaa.gov/maps-data/dataset/past-weather-zip-code-data-table\",\n        \"content\": \"\\u003CTITLE\\u003EPast Weather by Zip Code - Data Table | NOAA Climate.gov\\u003C/TITLE\\u003E\\u003CA\\u003EHome\\u003C/A\\u003E\\u003CA\\u003EMaps \\u0026 Data\\u003C/A\\u003E\\u003CA\\u003EDataset Gallery\\u003C/A\\u003E\\u003CH1\\u003EPast Weather by Zip Code - Data Table\\u003C/H1\\u003EClimate Data Online - Daily Summaries\\u003CP\\u003EHow much rain fell over the weekend? What was the temperature\\u00A0over the last few weeks?\\u00A0Tables of daily weather observations can answer these common questions.\\u003C/P\\u003E\\u003CH3\\u003EWhere do these data come from?\\u003C/H3\\u003E\\u003CP\\u003E\\u003CA\\u003EDaily summaries of past weather by location\\u003C/A\\u003E come from the Global Historical Climatology Network daily (\\u003CA\\u003EGHCNd\\u003C/A\\u003E) database and are accessed through the Climate Data Online (\\u003CA\\u003ECDO\\u003C/A\\u003E) interface, both of which are managed and maintained by \\u003CA\\u003ENOAA NCEI\\u003C/A\\u003E.\\u003C/P\\u003E\\u003CP\\u003EGHCNd includes daily observations from automated and human-facilitated weather stations across the United States and around the world. Observations can include weather variables such as maximum and minimum temperatures, total precipitation, snowfall, and depth of snow on ground. However, not all stations record all variables; about half the stations only report precipitation. Searching by zip code will yield no results if there is no weather station within that zip code, but you can easily expand your search to a city or county.\\u003C/P\\u003E\\u003CP\\u003EIf you have further questions or comments about the GHCN data or the Climate Data Online interface, you can send an email to NOAA NCEI at \\u003CA\\u003Encei.orders@noaa.gov\\u003C/A\\u003E or call them at 1-828-271-4800.\\u003C/P\\u003E\\u003CH3\\u003EWhat can I do with these data?\\u003C/H3\\u003E\\u003CUL\\u003E\\u003CLI\\u003ECheck records of past weather: explore how hot or cold it got through the week, how much rain or snow/sleet/hail fell, and how deep any snow was on the ground.\\nCheck what the weather was like on specific dates in history: did a snowstorm affect voter turnout on an election day? What was the weather on dates that are important to you?\\u003C/LI\\u003E\\u003C/UL\\u003E\\u003CUL\\u003E\\u003CLI\\u003EHow-To\\n\\u003CB\\u003EHow do I use the site?\\u003C/B\\u003E\\nNOTE: You may want to print these instructions so you can read them while you perform each step in another browser tab.\\nGo to the \\u003CA\\u003EClimate Data Online Search page\\u003C/A\\u003E (opens in a new tab)\\nUnder Select Weather Observation Type/Dataset, select\\u00A0Daily Summaries. Under Select Data Range, click the calendar icon and select dates on the Start and End calendars to reflect your dates of interest. Then click APPLY. Under the Search for dropdown, select ZIP codes Enter the ZIP code\\u00A0of interest as the Search term, and then click Search.\\n\\u003CUL\\u003E\\u003CLI\\u003EUnder Select Weather Observation Type/Dataset, select \\u003CB\\u003EDaily Summaries.\\u003C/B\\u003E\\nUnder \\u003CB\\u003ESelect Data Range\\u003C/B\\u003E, click the calendar icon and select dates on the Start and End calendars to reflect your dates of interest. Then click \\u003CB\\u003EAPPLY\\u003C/B\\u003E.\\nUnder the \\u003CB\\u003ESearch for\\u003C/B\\u003E dropdown, select \\u003CB\\u003EZIP codes\\u003C/B\\u003E\\n\\u003CB\\u003EEnter the ZIP code\\u003C/B\\u003E of interest as the Search term, and then click \\u003CB\\u003ESearch\\u003C/B\\u003E.\\u003C/LI\\u003E\\u003C/UL\\u003E\\nYour search results show up in the left column with a map of\\u00A0your ZIP code on the right.\\nClick the orange ADD TO CART button in the left column (these data are free). Place your cursor over the Cart button in the upper right. Click the orange VIEW ALL ITEMS button to go to the Select Cart Options page..\\n\\u003CUL\\u003E\\u003CLI\\u003EClick the orange \\u003CB\\u003EADD TO CART\\u003C/B\\u003E button in the left column (these data are free).\\nPlace your cursor over the Cart button in the upper right. Click the orange \\u003CB\\u003EVIEW ALL ITEMS\\u003C/B\\u003E button to go to the Select Cart Options page..\\u003C/LI\\u003E\\u003C/UL\\u003E\\nOn the Select Cart Options page, continue with the default selections. Scroll to the bottom and click \\u003CB\\u003ECONTINUE\\u003C/B\\u003E.\\nOn the Review Order page, enter your email address (twice) and click \\u003CB\\u003ESUBMIT ORDER\\u003C/B\\u003E. You can also find Help links on this page.\\nThe \\u003CB\\u003EREQUEST SUBMITTED\\u003C/B\\u003E page offers further information\\nThe action will now move to your \\u003CB\\u003Eemail inbox\\u003C/B\\u003E. First, you\\u0027ll receive a notice that the request has been submitted. Usually, just a few minutes later, you\\u0027ll receive an email stating that your order has been processed. The second email contains a link for you to download the data you requested, in a multi-page data table. Check all pages to see the full range of data.\\n\\nData Access\\nData Format (s)\\nTXT (ASCII), CSV, PDF\\nDocumentation\\nDocumentation Type  Link \\u0026 Description  General  GHCN (Global Historical Climatology Network) \\u2013 Daily Documentation  General  GHCNd - About and Updates  Articles  GHCNd - Journal Articles\\nDocumentation Type\\nLink \\u0026 Description\\n\\u003CB\\u003EGeneral\\u003C/B\\u003E\\n\\u003CA\\u003EGHCN (Global Historical Climatology Network) \\u2013 Daily Documentation\\u003C/A\\u003E\\n\\u003CB\\u003EGeneral\\u003C/B\\u003E\\n\\u003CA\\u003EGHCNd - About and Updates\\u003C/A\\u003E\\n\\u003CB\\u003EArticles\\u003C/B\\u003E\\n\\u003CA\\u003EGHCNd - Journal Articles\\u003C/A\\u003E\\nTechnical\\nData Type\\nLand-based station\\nEssential Climate Variables\\nAir temperature,\\nScience Organization\\nNOAA NCEI\\nData Steward\\nGlobal Historical Climatology Network daily (GHCNd)\\nEmail\\nncei.orders@noaa.gov\\u003C/LI\\u003E\\u003C/UL\\u003EExample Image\\u003CBR\\u003EClick to see more detail\\u003CBR\\u003EDirect Link\\u003CA\\u003EClimate Data Online Search\\u003C/A\\u003ECoverage\\u003CBR\\u003EUS\\u003CMETA description=\\u0022How much rain fell over the weekend? What was the temperature over the last few weeks? Tables of daily weather observations can answer these common questions.\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C/META\\u003E\",\n        \"lastUpdatedAt\": \"2015-02-06T00:00:00.0000000\",\n        \"crawledAt\": \"2026-09-04T15:31:00.0000000Z\",\n        \"language\": \"en\",\n        \"isAdult\": false,\n        \"clickUrl\": \"https://api.microsoft.ai/ck/a?!\\u0026\\u0026p=df2bc484eaed76a0fcefea7ecb670e01c7b8b28425cb180a41c70760d8dc0217JmltdHM9MTc4ODU2NDY3MSZpZ3VpZD1kYmVlODQ4MS0wYTg2LTVkNWEtY2Q3OS1lOGYwNDQ4YmI2YTEmbGdtYXA9UDJOcFpEMHlOa0kxTTBaRU1EUTVNamswTXpORU9FRXhOalE0TURNeU9VSXhNVEJHUWlaaGNIQnVjejFFWlhaRmVDWnJQVEV3TURrbQ\\u0026ptn=10\\u0026ntb=1\\u0026u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly9wcm9kLTAxLWFzZy13d3ctY2xpbWF0ZS53b2Mubm9hYS5nb3YvbWFwcy1kYXRhL2RhdGFzZXQvcGFzdC13ZWF0aGVyLXppcC1jb2RlLWRhdGEtdGFibGU\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"querySignals\": {\n      \"freshness\": false\n    },\n    \"traceId\": \"dbee84810a865d5acd79e8f0448bb6a1\"\n  }\n}\n","status":"completed"},{"type":"message","id":"msg_088fa09f0ed754bc006a9b54c2a70c8195953d6dbe74f9b2a1","agent_reference":{"type":"agent_reference","name":"cs-e2e-tests-client","version":"24"},"response_id":"resp_088fa09f0ed754bc006a9b54bdae608195af404a34a310cba7","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Here’s a summary of weather history in Centralia, Pennsylvania (ZIP: 17927), covering both recent and longer-term observations:\n\n---\n\n### **Monthly Averages (Centralia Climate Data)**\nSource: [PlantMaps.com Centralia Climate Data](https://www.plantmaps.com/en/clim/f/us/pennsylvania/centralia/climate-data)\n\n| Month      | Avg. Low (°F) | Avg. High (°F) | Avg. Precip (inches) |\n|------------|---------------|---------------|----------------------|\n| January    | 17.5          | 32.5          | 3.69                 |\n| February   | 18.6          | 35.0          | 2.83                 |\n| March      | 25.7          | 43.6          | 4.19                 |\n| April      | 36.9          | 56.9          | 4.13                 |\n| May        | 47.3          | 67.6          | 4.42                 |\n| June       | 56.0          | 75.3          | 4.81                 |\n| July       | 60.6          | 80.4          | 5.01                 |\n| August     | 58.8          | 78.7          | 4.57                 |\n| September  | 51.8          | 72.0          | 5.38                 |\n| October    | 41.3          | 60.2          | 5.06                 |\n| November   | 31.3          | 47.5          | 3.77                 |\n| December   | 23.1          | 37.3          | 4.08                 |\n| **Annual** | **39.1**      | **57.3**      | **51.9**             |\n\n- **Climate: Humid Continental Mild Summer, Wet All Year (Köppen: Dfb)**\n- **Annual Frost Days:** 100–125 days\n- **Growing season:** Last frost May 1–10, first frost Oct. 11–20\n\n---\n\n### **Hourly & Daily Weather Records**\n- Full hourly/weather history is available from July 2008 onwards via [World Weather Online](https://www.worldweatheronline.com/v2/historical-weather.aspx?q=17927).\n- Example (recent 24-hour period):\n  - Max temperature: 84°F\n  - Min temperature: 69°F\n  - Average: 76°F\n  - Barometric pressure: ~30 inHg\n  - Humidity: ranges from ~46–81%\n  - Wind speeds: typically light, gusts up to ~18 mph.\n\n---\n\n**Historical data over the years—September 3rd (Sample)**\n| Year | Max (°F) | Min (°F) | Rain (in) | Humidity (%) | Cloud (%) |\n|------|----------|----------|-----------|--------------|-----------|\n| 2009 | 78       | 49       | 0.0       | 75           | 13        |\n| 2015 | 87       | 67       | 0.1       | 73           | 23        |\n| 2017 | 65       | 55       | 0.5       | 92           | 72        |\n| 2023 | 87       | 62       | 0.0       | 67           | 14        |\n| 2026 | 85       | 65       | 8.4       | 85           | 93        |\n\n---\n\n### **How to Get Full Historical Data (NOAA/NCEI)**\n- For detailed, downloadable daily summaries (temperature, precipitation, snow), use the [NCEI Past Weather Tool](https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/past-weather/US%20weather%20by%20zip%20code) and enter Centralia’s zip (17927). Data includes land-based station records since 1763 (varying by station).\n- You can also use [NOAA’s Climate Data Online](https://prod-01-asg-www-climate.woc.noaa.gov/maps-data/dataset/past-weather-zip-code-data-table).\n\n---\n\n### **Recent Daily Example** (from [LocalConditions.com](https://www.localconditions.com/us/centralia/pennsylvania/weather/past/)):\n- May 8th: High 68°F, Low 54°F, Rainfall 2.55in, overcast to heavy rain showers, humidity up to 95%.\n- Earlier days show similar trends—periods of heavy rain, high humidity, moderate wind, and typical continental climate temperature swings.\n\n---\n\n### **Summary**\n**Centralia, PA** features a humid continental climate, with warm, wet summers and cold, snowy winters. Annual precipitation is substantial (~52 in/yr), and weather history is available in detail from both public government and commercial sources. If you’re after specific dates or types of weather (e.g., snowstorms, droughts), the NOAA records and Plantmaps climate data make it easy to search by date or climate trend.\n\n---\n\n**References for more details & downloadable records:**\n- [WorldWeatherOnline Centralia History](https://www.worldweatheronline.com/v2/historical-weather.aspx?q=17927)\n- [Centralia Climate Data (PlantMaps)](https://www.plantmaps.com/en/clim/f/us/pennsylvania/centralia/climate-data)\n- [LocalConditions.com Past Weather](https://www.localconditions.com/us/centralia/pennsylvania/weather/past/)\n- [NOAA Past Weather for Centralia](https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/past-weather/US%20weather%20by%20zip%20code)\n\nIf you want a CSV or specific date-range dataset, let me know!","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"status":"completed"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"in_memory","reasoning":{"context":null,"effort":null,"summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":true,"temperature":1.0,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"required","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[{"type":"web_iq_preview","project_connection_id":"/subscriptions/bfd9f30e-252d-4fc8-823c-f27d994fc8b7/resourceGroups/rg-agentsv2-ga-bugbash/providers/Microsoft.CognitiveServices/accounts/agentsv2-ga-bugbash-tip/projects/project2/connections/WebIQConnection","require_approval":"never"}],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":1.0,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":93516,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":2688},"output_tokens":1293,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":0},"total_tokens":94809},"user":null,"metadata":{},"agent_reference":{"type":"agent_reference","name":"cs-e2e-tests-client","version":"24"}},"sequence_number":204}
